<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow> breaks `sf`
        deploy at source conversion with the misleading error "unable to find matching parent
        xml file". Precedent: flows/Counter_Offer_Notify.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-14 (Phase 3, observation 7). THIS FILE WAS NOT IN THE SPEC, NOT IN
        THE REQUIREMENTS DOC AND NOT IN THE BUILD BRIEF. IT WAS FOUND BY SWEEPING flows/ FOR
        Negotiation_Status__c, AND LEFT ALONE IT WOULD HAVE FAILED SILENTLY AND PERMANENTLY.
        =====================================================================

        WHAT IT DOES. After-save on Contract_Review__c: notifies the Acquisitions_Team group that
        a PSA is ready for signature. doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true, so it fires
        on the TRANSITION INTO the value, not on every subsequent save.

        THE DEFECT. Its only entry criterion was Negotiation_Status__c = 'Ready for Execution',
        with NO record-type criterion, so it has always served BOTH PSA record types. Phase 3
        gives Acquisition_PSA its own sequence - Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed - and
        removes 'Ready for Execution' from that record type. Every acquisition PSA would then
        pass from Negotiation straight to Signed to Executed WITHOUT EVER MATCHING THIS FLOW, so
        the "PSA ready for execution" notification would stop reaching the Acquisitions team for
        every acquisition deal, for ever, with nothing erroring and no test failing. A
        notification that stops arriving is indistinguishable from a quiet week.

        THE FIX AND WHY IT IS AN OR RATHER THAN A SWAP. 'Signed' is the acquisition analogue of
        'Ready for Execution' - the document is final and signatures are being collected, the
        step immediately before 'Executed' in both sequences. But Disposition_PSA STILL RUNS ON
        'Ready for Execution' and is untouched by Phase 3 (decision O3), so swapping the literal
        would simply move the outage onto the sell-side path. filterLogic is therefore 'or' over
        both values. This is additive and correct on BOTH sides of the Phase 3 row migration, so
        it ships at P3-D1 rather than in the migration window.

        ⚠ THE TWO VALUES ARE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE IN PRACTICE - no record type exposes both - so
        the OR cannot double-notify. Disposition_PSA's behaviour is byte-for-byte unchanged: it
        can never reach 'Signed'.

        ⚠ THE NOTIFICATION TITLE IS DELIBERATELY NOT REWORDED. "PSA ready for execution" reads
        correctly for 'Signed' as well as for 'Ready for Execution', and it is shared by both
        record types; rewording it to name one sequence's vocabulary would make it wrong for the
        other. Same reasoning as the Stage__c labels (PSA Drafting / Review / Contract Execution)
        being left buy-side-shaped in Disposition_PSA's own header.

        ⚠ 'Executed' IS DELIBERATELY NOT ADDED HERE. It is the handoff, owned by
        ContractExecutionService, and it already has its own downstream notifications.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Notify_Ready</name>
        <label>Notify Ready</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <actionName>GroupNotifier</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>recipientGroup</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Acquisitions_Team</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>title</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>PSA ready for execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>body</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Name</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>targetRecordId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>GroupNotifier</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>PSA Ready Notify {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>PSA Ready Notify</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Notify_Ready</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>or</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Negotiation_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Ready for Execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Negotiation_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Signed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Contract_Review__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
